---
// Terms. Copy: advisory_based_specs/02_Replacement_Copy.md §19, with the
// bracketed items completed from the owner's decisions on 2026-09-27:
//   - Operator stays under the PainToBuild name.
//   - Scope, timing, results deadline, payment and what happens if no test is
//     run are set in each client's written agreement, not on this page.
//   - Free cancellation before work starts.
//   - Guides (Brief and Kit): sales final, apart from legal rights and
//     Gumroad's buyer protection.
// This is not legal advice. Update the review date below only when the page
// is actually reviewed.
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Kicker from '../components/content/Kicker.astro';
import { EMAIL } from '../lib/routes';

const title = 'Terms for reviews, guides and tools | PainToBuild';
const description = 'Read what a PainToBuild review or resource purchase includes, how the work is agreed and which payment, delivery and cancellation terms apply.';
const lastReviewed = { iso: '2026-09-27', label: 'September 27, 2026' };
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} ogImagePath="/open-graph/terms.png">
  <section class="wrap section prose">
    <Kicker>Terms</Kicker>
    <h1>Terms for reviews, guides and tools</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      These terms cover the reviews, guides and tools provided by PainToBuild, which is run by one
      person under the PainToBuild name.
    </p>
    <p>
      For a personal review, your written agreement adds the details of your review. If your
      agreement and this page differ, your agreement applies.
    </p>

    <h2>Personal reviews</h2>
    <p>
      Before I start, you and I agree in writing on the question, the work, the price and the
      delivery date. The agreement lists what you receive and what is not included. It also says
      when the later results review will take place.
    </p>
    <p>Sending an inquiry does not start paid work. Any extra work needs a separate agreement.</p>
    <p>You remain responsible for running your business and carrying out the test unless the agreement says otherwise.</p>

    <h2>Information and timing</h2>
    <p>I need the agreed information to carry out the review.</p>
    <p>
      If information arrives late, is missing or is not suitable, I will tell you, and the delivery
      date may need to move. Any change to the schedule is agreed with you in writing.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions and the later review</h2>
    <p>
      The Founder Decision Review includes one round of questions about the written review and one
      later review of the test results.
    </p>
    <p>
      Your agreement says how long you have to send questions and results, which results to send,
      and what happens if the test is not run.
    </p>

    <h2>Payment, cancellation and refunds</h2>
    <p>Your agreement says how and when you pay, and when work is considered started.</p>
    <p>
      If you or I cancel before work starts, you pay nothing, and anything you have already
      paid is refunded. After work starts, cancellation and refunds follow your agreement.
    </p>
    <p>This does not affect any rights you have by law.</p>

    <h2>Guides and tools</h2>
    <p>
      The Brief and Kit are separate products. Each product page lists the files, edition and
      price. Future volumes are separate purchases unless the listing says they are included.
    </p>
    <p>
      The guides are digital files delivered through Gumroad, which is the seller of record for
      these purchases. Sales are final and not refundable, except where the law requires a refund
      or under Gumroad's own buyer protection.
    </p>

    <h2>What the advice can promise</h2>
    <p>
      My advice is based on the information available at the time of the review. Sometimes the
      next step is more research rather than a change to the product.
    </p>
    <p>A review cannot guarantee customers, revenue, funding or a successful business.</p>

    <h2>Your information and work</h2>
    <p>The <a href="/privacy/">privacy page</a> and your agreement explain how your information is handled.</p>
    <p>
      You can use your written review for your own business. I do not publish your material or
      results without your separate permission.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions and corrections</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a> if you have a concern or notice something that
      needs correcting. Include the relevant page, product or review.
    </p>

    <p class="reviewed">Last reviewed <time datetime={lastReviewed.iso}>{lastReviewed.label}</time>.</p>

    <ul class="link-list">
      <li><a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a></li>
      <li><a href="/advisory/">What the review includes</a></li>
      <li><a href="/contact/">Contact me</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .section { padding-block: var(--s7) var(--s8); }
  .reviewed { color: var(--muted); font-size: var(--t-caption); margin-top: var(--s7) !important; }
</style>
